# sweep-2d-gpu.steps -- the 2D sweep for comparing the SDL_GPU backend (-gpu)
# against GL (#340 P1c onward).  Frames 01-04 are tools/sweep-2d.steps'; 05 adds
# a console frame whose text is the same on both renderers (04's boot log is
# not: it names the renderer), 06 the menu again.
#
# Run the SAME binary both ways, with gamma 1 on both:
#
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-2d-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/2d-gl \
#       $DATA +gamma 1
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd or nvidia_icd json> STEPS=tools/sweep-2d-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/2d-gpu $DATA -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 \
#       -gpushaders <build>/generated/spirv +gamma 1
#
# Why gamma 1: the demo's default.cfg sets gamma 0.75, which GL applies in the
# post-process chain, and that chain is P4 -- off under -gpu.  At gamma 1 GL
# skips the chain too, so both sides draw the 2D straight to the frame.
#
# Compare with sweep-2d.steps' two cursor masks plus 8,584-300,595: the main
# menu's footer names the renderer ("Desktop OpenGL 4.3" / "SDL_GPU").  What
# is left is isolated columns inside text rows, where a pixel centre lands on
# a glyph texel boundary and the two implementations round the nearest texel
# differently, plus (NVIDIA) 1-level blend rounding under the translucent
# console; 04 differs by its text.  Measured at P1c, llvmpipe GL vs lavapipe
# -gpu, pixels off by more than 2/255: 63 on 01-03 and 06 (PSNR 51.7 dB),
# 610 on 05 (47.2 dB).

sleep 6
shot 01-main-menu
key Down
sleep 1
shot 02-menu-moved
key Return
sleep 2
shot 03-submenu
key Escape
sleep 1
key Escape
sleep 1
shot 04-back-to-main
# 04 leaves the console up with focus, so this types straight into it.
enter clear
enter echo The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789
enter echo HEXEN II -- SDL_GPU sweep: ()[]{}<>+-*/=_.,:;!?
sleep 2
shot 05-console-fixed
key Escape
sleep 2
shot 06-menu-again
